We may receive personal data about you from:
• sign-in providers, such as Google, when you choose to sign in with them, including your name, email address and profile picture;
• institutions and partners, for example confirmations or updates about your interest, application or eligibility;
• a parent, guardian or other person who registers or manages an Account on your behalf;
• publicly available sources and data providers, where the law allows.

We may combine this data with the data we already hold about you and use it for the purposes described in this Policy.

We use personal data for the following purposes:
• to create and manage your Account, verify your identity and keep the Service secure;
• to provide the Service, including search, comparison, saved items, application tracking, nearest-campus results and personalized recommendations, matches and estimates;
• to share your data with institutions and partners as described in this Policy, so that they can contact you and offer you programs, admissions, scholarships, events and services;
• to send you service messages, and marketing and promotional communications from UniLink and its partners, subject to your right to opt out;
• to measure and analyse use of the Service, conduct research, develop new features, and improve our content, algorithms and models;
• to produce aggregated and de-identified statistics, reports, rankings and insights, and to use, publish, sell and license them;
• to support commercial relationships with institutions and partners, including demand analysis, reporting and the evaluation and delivery of partnership services;
• to moderate content, prevent fraud and abuse, enforce our Terms and limits (such as free-search limits), and protect the rights, safety and property of UniLink, our Users and others;
• to comply with legal obligations and respond to lawful requests from authorities;
• in connection with any sale, merger, financing or reorganization of our business.

Subject to the conditions and exceptions in the PDPL, you have the right to:
• know what personal data about you we hold and obtain a copy of it;
• have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected or completed;
• have your personal data erased or its processing restricted, where the law provides for this;
• withdraw your consent to further processing at any time;
• object to processing, including processing for direct marketing;
• be informed of any breach of your personal data as required by law.

You can update much of your data yourself from your Profile, Saved and Applications pages. For other requests, contact us using the details below. We may need to verify your identity before responding, and we will respond within the period required by law. Where the law allows, we may decline or limit a request, for example where data must be kept for legal reasons or where a request is manifestly unfounded or excessive.

You must not, and must not help or allow anyone else to:
• copy, scrape, crawl, harvest, index, download in bulk or otherwise extract Content, listings, fees, scores or other data from the Platform by any automated or manual means, except through normal use of the Service’s interface for your personal research;
• build, train or improve any database, directory, competing service, dataset or artificial-intelligence or machine-learning model using Content or data obtained from the Platform;
• reproduce, republish, frame, mirror, sell, license or commercially exploit any part of the Service or its Content;
• reverse engineer, decompile or attempt to discover the source code, structure or algorithms of the Service, except where the law expressly permits this;
• bypass, disable or interfere with security features, usage limits, access controls or the limits on free searches;
• introduce viruses, malware or any harmful code, or attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Service, other Accounts, or our systems;
• overload, disrupt or impair the Service, for example through denial-of-service attacks or excessive automated requests;
• create Accounts by automated means or under false pretences, or create multiple Accounts to evade restrictions;
• use the Service to send unsolicited messages or advertising, or to collect Personal Data about other Users;
• post fake ratings or reviews, or manipulate rankings, ratings or statistics;
• use the Service in breach of any law, including laws on data protection, consumer protection, intellectual property and cybercrime.

We may investigate any suspected breach and take any action we consider appropriate, including removing content, suspending or closing Accounts, blocking access, and reporting the matter to the competent authorities.

By accepting these Terms you give your express, specific and informed consent, and where you are under 18 your parent or guardian gives it on your behalf, for UniLink to collect, store, use, analyse, combine, transfer, disclose and share your Personal Data and User Content for the purposes and with the recipients described in these Terms and the Privacy Policy. In summary, and without limiting the Privacy Policy, you agree that UniLink may:
• use your data to provide, personalize and improve the Service, including recommendations, matching, fee and admission estimates, nearest-campus results and comparisons;
• share your profile, academic details, preferences, interests, saved items and contact details with Institutions and Partners, so that they can contact you about their programs, admissions, scholarships, events and services, assess your eligibility, or offer you opportunities;
• share data with service providers who host, store, secure, analyse, support, email or otherwise process data for us, and with our affiliates, advisers and professional consultants;
• share and license data with Partners for marketing, advertising, research, analytics and commercial purposes, including to measure demand for programs and to help Institutions plan their admissions and marketing;
• use your contact details to send you information, offers and marketing messages from UniLink and its Partners, subject to your right to opt out of marketing at any time;
• create, use, publish, sell and license aggregated, statistical and de-identified data and insights derived from your data and the data of other Users;
• transfer your data, as part of the Service’s assets, to any buyer, investor, successor or merger partner in connection with a sale, merger, reorganization, financing or transfer of all or part of UniLink’s business;
• transfer your data to and process it in countries outside the Arab Republic of Egypt, where our service providers or Partners operate, subject to the safeguards required by law;
• disclose your data where required by law, court order or a competent authority, or where needed to protect the rights, safety and property of UniLink, our Users or others.

You may withdraw your consent at any time as described in the Privacy Policy. Withdrawal does not affect processing, sharing or licensing that took place before you withdrew, does not affect data that has already been aggregated or de-identified, and may mean that we can no longer provide some or all of the Service to you.
